      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Transfer to the airport of Campo Grande for your flight to São Luís. Arrival, meeting at the airport and transfer to the hotel. \n\nSão Luís is the only Brazilian state capital founded by the French who ruled over parts of Brazil until they were defeated by the Portuguese. Founded in 1612, the city is named after French King Louis XIII. Later, it was also occupied by the Dutch, until the Portuguese colonizers took over.\n\nThe city is an island that is enchanting by its beauty, legends and history.  Surrounded by warm water beaches all year, São Luís City, World Heritage Site since 1997, offers visitors the centuries old streets with colonial buildings and tiles. "
